                                                                  PAGE 2                                               ÄISK ÄOCTOR ÄOCUMENTATION               1.0    ÉNTRODUCTION           ÔHE OBJECTIVE OF THE PROGRAM 'ÄISK ÄOCTOR' IS TO  ALLOW  EASY           MANIPULATION OF DATA  AND  CORRECTION  OF  ERRORS  ON  FLOPPY           DISKETTES.  ÔHE OPERATION OF THE  PROGRAM  HAS  INTENTIONALLY           BEEN KEPT SIMPLE TO ALLOW MORE USERS THE ABILITY TO MAKE  USE           OF IT'S CAPABILITIES.  ÁLTHOUGH THE USE OF  THE  PROGRAM  HAS           BEEN KEPT SIMPLE THE DATA THAT CAN BE ALTERED ON  THE  FLOPPY           IS  IN  A  SPECIFIC  ORDER.   ÏNE  OF  THE  BEST  SOURCES  OF           INFORMATION ABOUT HOW DATA IS WRITTEN AND STORED ON A  FLOPPY           DISKETTE IS THE MANUAL WHICH CAME WITH YOUR DISK DRIVE.           ÔHIS PROGRAM HAS THE POWER  TO  RUIN  DISKETTES  AS  WELL  AS           RECLAIM INFORMATION  FROM THEM.  ÉT IS FOR THIS  REASON  THAT           WE STRONGLY SUGGEST YOU BECOME FAMILIAR  WITH  THE  DIRECTORY           STRUCTURE AND FILE CHAINING FORMAT COVERED IN YOUR DISK DRIVE           MANUAL.           ÔHROUGHOUT THIS MANUAL YOU WILL SEE '[RETURN]' THIS INDICATES           THAT THE RETURN KEY SHOULD BE DEPRESSED.                                                                  PAGE 3                                               ÄISK ÄOCTOR ÄOCUMENTATION               2.0    ÌOADING AND ÒUNNING ÉNSTRUCTIONS           'ÄÉÓË ÄÏÃÔÏÒ.ÔÅÄ' WILL WORK ON THE ÃOMMODORE 16 AND ÃOMMODORE           ÐLUS/4 COMPUTERS AND IS WRITTEN IN MACHINE  LANGUAGE  WITH  A           ONE LINE BASIC DRIVER.  ÉN THIS WAY LOADING IS VERY SIMPLE AS           FOLLOWS :                      ÄÌÏÁÄ "ÄÉÓË ÄÏÃÔÏÒ.ÔÅÄ"  [RETURN]           ÔHIS STATEMENT WILL LOAD THE PROGRAM INTO  THE  MEMORY  SPACE           NORMALLY OCCUPIED BY BASIC PROGRAMS.  ÉF YOU WERE TO ASK  FOR           A 'ÌÉÓÔ [RETURN]' YOU WOULD SEE :                      16 SYS (4128)           ÔO START 'ÄISK ÄOCTOR' TYPE IN 'ÒÕÎ [RETURN].'  ÁT THIS POINT           YOU WILL SEE A SCREEN WITH THE TITLE OF THE  PROGRAM,  A  FEW           INSTRUCTONS AND YOU ARE READY TO GO.           ÔHERE ARE SEVERAL COMMANDS AND FUNCTIONS THAT ÄISK ÄOCTOR CAN           PERFORM.  ÉF  YOU  ARE  JUST  GETTING  STARTED  AND  WISH  TO           EXPERIMENT,  USE  A  DISKETTE  WHICH  DOES  NOT  CONTAIN  ANY           VALUABLE INFORMATION.  ÁLTERING INFORMATION ON  THE  DISKETTE           CAN CORRUPT THE ENTIRE DISKETTE.           ÔHE COMMANDS IN SECTION 3.0 OF THIS MANUAL WILL  DETAIL  WHAT           EACH OF THE COMMANDS ARE CAPABLE OF DOING.  ÉN EVERY  COMMAND           AS A PRECAUTION THE ÓÔÏÐ KEY WILL EXIT  THE  COMMAND  WITHOUT           THE FUNCTION OF THE COMMAND TAKING PLACE.           ÎÏÔÅ : ÄISK ÄOCTOR CAN IRREPARABLY MODIFY A DISKETTE'S DATA.                                                                  PAGE 4                                               ÄISK ÄOCTOR ÄOCUMENTATION               3.0    ÃOMMANDS               3.Á  '@'  ÃHANGE BYTE UNDER CURSOR           ÔHE CHANGE BYTE UNDER CURSOR IS ENVOKED   BY  DEPRESSING  THE           '@' KEY.           ×HEN THE CHANGE BYTE COMMAND IS CALLED A PROMPT IS PRINTED IN           THE MESSAGE BUFFER UNDER THE DATA BOX AS FOLLOWS :                      ÃÈÁÎÇÅ ÂÙÔÅ ÎÅ× ÖÁÌÕÅ [Ä/$È]=           ÔHE PROGRAM NOW WANTS YOU TO INPUT  EITHER  A  DECIMAL  VALUE           BETWEEN 0-255 [RETURN] OR A HEXIDECIMAL VALUE  BETWEEN  00-FF           PRECEEDED BY A '$' FOLLOWED BY [RETURN].  ÁFTER INPUTTING THE           VALUE THE PROGRAM WILL CHANGE THAT BYTE UNDER THE  CURSOR  ON           THE SCREEN, CHANGE THIS CHARACTER'S COLOR TO RED  AND  CHANGE           THE BYTE IN THE DISK DRIVE BUFFER.  ÔHIS CHANGE WILL  NOT  BE           WRITTEN TO THE FLOPPY DISKETTE UNTIL THE EXECUTION OF THE  'Ò           REWRITE' COMMAND DISCUSSED LATER IN SECTION 3.Ì.  ÔHE  ÃHANGE           BYTE COMMAND CAN BE EXITED WITH THE USE OF THE ÓÔÏÐ KEY.               3.Â  'Ô'  ÔEXT MODE           ÔHE TEXT MODE IS ENVOKED BY DEPRESSING THE 'T' KEY.           ×HEN THE TEXT MODE COMMAND IS CALLED THE SCREEN BORDER  COLOR           BECOMES ORANGE AND A PROMPT IS PRINTED IN THE MESSAGE  BUFFER           UNDER THE DATA BOX AS FOLLOWS :                      ÔÅØÔ ÍÏÄÅ : ÐRESS ÒETURN TO ÅXIT           ÔHE PROGRAM NOW ALLOWS YOU TO ALTER THE DATA BY SIMPLY TYPING           ON THE KEYBOARD.  ÄATA MAY BE TYPED IN UPPER  CASE  OR  LOWER           CASE WITH REVERSE ON OR OFF.  ÙOU MAY USE THE CURSOR KEYS  TO           POSITION THE CURSOR ANYWHERE IN THE DATA BOX.  ÁS  EACH  BYTE           IS TYPED THE BYTE IS CHANGED UNDER THE CURSOR ON THE  SCREEN,           THAT CHARACTER'S COLOR IS CHANGED TO RED AND THE BYTE IN  THE           DISK DRIVE BUFFER IS CHANGED. ÁS IN THE ÃHANGE  BYTE  COMMAND           THIS CHANGE WILL NOT BE WRITTEN TO THE FLOPPY DISKETTE  UNTIL           THE EXECUTION OF THE 'Ò REWRITE' COMMAND DISCUSSED  LATER  IN           SECTION 3.Ì.  ÁFTER STRIKING THE [RETURN]  KEY  TO  EXIT  THE           ÔEXT MODE THE MESSAGE IS REMOVED  FROM  THE  SCREEN  AND  THE           BORDER COLOR RETURNED TO PURPLE.  ÔHE ÔEXT MODE CAN  ALSO  BE           EXITED BY USING THE ÓÔÏÐ KEY.                                                                  PAGE 5                                               ÄISK ÄOCTOR ÄOCUMENTATION               3.0    ÃOMMANDS               3.Ã  'Ä'  ÄRIVE TO ACCESS           ÔHE ÄRIVE COMMAND IS ENVOKED BY DEPRESSING THE 'D' KEY.           ×HEN THE DRIVE COMMAND IS CALLED THE CURSOR WILL BE  FLASHING           ON THE NUMBER TO THE RIGHT OF ÄRIVE IN THE UPPER  INFORMATION           BOX.  ÁT THIS POINT YOU HAVE SEVERAL OPTIONS.  ÏNE OPTION  IS           TO ENTER A '0' OR A '1'  TO  SPECIFY  THE  DRIVE  TO  ACCESS.           ÁNOTHER OPTION IS TO ENTER 'U' TO CHANGE THE  UNIT  THAT  THE           PROGRAM WILL ACCESS.  ÔHE 'U' COMMAND IS DETAILED IN THE NEXT           SECTION 3.Ä.  ÈELP CAN ALSO BE OBTAINED FROM THE DRIVE OPTION           BY DEPRESSING THE 'ÈÅÌÐ' KEY.  ÉF THE NUMBER ALREADY CONTAINS           THE VALUE YOU REQUIRE THEN SIMPLY STRIKE THE [RETURN] KEY AND           THE PROGRAM WILL GO TO THE DISK DRIVE, GET THE DATA FROM THIS           BLOCK AND DISPLAY IT ON THE SCREEN.  ÔHE PROGRAM CAN ALSO  BE           EXITED BY USING THE ÓÔÏÐ KEY FROM THE DRIVE COMMAND.               3.Ä  'Õ'  ÕNIT TO ACCESS           ÔHE ÕNIT COMMAND IS ENVOKED BY DEPRESSING THE 'U' KEY.           ×HEN THE UNIT COMMAND IS CALLED THE CURSOR WILL  BE  FLASHING           ON THE NUMBER TO THE RIGHT OF 'ÕNIT' NEAR THE BOTTOM  OF  THE           SCREEN.  ÔHE UNIT CAN BE ANY NUMBER FROM 8 TO  15  INCLUSIVE.           ÉF YOU HAVE A SECOND DRIVE CONNECTED  AS  UNIT  9  THEN  THIS           COMMAND WILL INSTRUCT  'ÄISK  ÄOCTOR'  TO  ACCESS  THAT  DISK           DRIVE.  ÉF THE NUMBER ALREADY CONTAINS THE VALUE YOU  REQUIRE           THEN SIMPLY STRIKE THE [RETURN] KEY.                                                                  PAGE 6                                               ÄISK ÄOCTOR ÄOCUMENTATION               3.0    ÃOMMANDS               3.Å  'Â'  ÂLOCK           ÔHE ÂLOCK COMMAND IS ENVOKED BY DEPRESSING THE 'B' KEY.           ×HEN THE BLOCK COMMAND IS CALLED THE CURSOR WILL BE  FLASHING           ON THE FIRST CHARACTER OF THE TWO DIGIT NUMBER TO  THE  RIGHT           OF 'ÔRACK' IN THE UPPER INFORMATION BOX.  ÔHE PROGRAM IS  NOW           WAITING FOR YOU TO INPUT A TRACK NUMBER.  ÁFTER THE TRACK HAS           BEEN INPUT THE CURSOR IMMEDIATELY  MOVES  TO  THE  TWO  DIGIT           NUMBER TO THE RIGHT OF 'ÓECTOR' IN THE UPPER INFORMATION BOX.           ÔHE PROGRAM IS NOW WAITING FOR YOU TO INPUT A SECTOR  NUMBER.           ×HEN THE BLOCK HAS BEEN INPUT  (IE.  ÔRACK  AND  ÓECTOR)  THE           PROGRAM WILL GO TO THE DISK DRIVE , GET THE DATA FROM THE NEW           BLOCK AND DISPLAY IT ON THE SCREEN.  ÔHE PROGRAM CAN ALSO  BE           EXITED BY USING THE ÓÔÏÐ KEY WHILE  INPUTTING  THE  TRACK  OR           SECTOR.               3.Æ  '+'  ÉNCREMENT SECTOR           ÔHE ÉNCREMENT SECTOR COMMAND IS ENVOKED BY DEPRESSING THE '+'           KEY.           ×HEN THE INCREMENT SECTOR COMMAND IS CALLED THE YOU WILL  SEE           THE TWO DIGIT NUMBER TO THE RIGHT OF 'ÓECTOR'  IN  THE  UPPER           INFORMATION BOX  BECOME  INCREMENTED  BY  ONE.   ÁFTER   THIS           INCREMENT THE PROGRAM WILL GO TO THE DISK  DRIVE  ,  GET  THE           DATA FROM THE NEW BLOCK AND DISPLAY IT ON THE  SCREEN.   ÔHIS           COMMAND IS USEFUL IF YOU WANT TO  LOOK  THROUGH  ALL  OF  THE           SECTORS IN A PARTICULAR TRACK.               3.Ç  '-'  ÄECREMENT SECTOR           ÔHE ÄECREMENT SECTOR COMMAND IS ENVOKED BY DEPRESSING THE '-'           KEY.           ×HEN THE DECREMENT SECTOR COMMAND IS CALLED THE YOU WILL  SEE           THE TWO DIGIT NUMBER TO THE RIGHT OF 'ÓECTOR'  IN  THE  UPPER           INFORMATION BOX  BECOME  DECREMENTED  BY  ONE.   ÁFTER   THIS           DECREMENT THE PROGRAM WILL GO TO THE DISK  DRIVE  ,  GET  THE           DATA FROM THE NEW BLOCK AND DISPLAY IT ON  THE  SCREEN.   ÔHE           DECREMENT COMMAND WILL ONLY DECREMENT THE SECTOR TO  A  VALUE           OF 00.  ÔHIS COMMAND IS USEFUL IF YOU WANT  TO  LOOK  THROUGH           ALL OF THE SECTORS IN A PARTICULAR TRACK.                                                                  PAGE 7                                               ÄISK ÄOCTOR ÄOCUMENTATION               3.0    ÃOMMANDS               3.È  'Ñ'  ÑUIT           ÔHE ÑUIT COMMAND IS ENVOKED BY DEPRESSING THE 'Q' KEY.           ×HEN THE QUIT FUNCTION IS CALLED ALL OF THE  DISK  FILES  ARE           CLOSED AND CONTROL IS RETURNED TO DIRECT BASIC MODE.               3.É  'ÓÔÏÐ'           ÔHE ÓTOP COMMAND IS ENVOKED BY DEPRESSING THE 'ÓÔÏÐ' KEY.           ÔHIS COMMAND IS IDENTICAL TO THE ÑUIT COMMAND.  ×HEN THE STOP           FUNCTION IS CALLED ALL OF  THE  DISK  FILES  ARE  CLOSED  AND           CONTROL IS RETURNED TO THE DIRECT BASIC MODE.               3.Ê  'Ê'  ÊUMP           ÔHE ÊUMP COMMAND IS ENVOKED BY DEPRESSING THE 'J' KEY.           ×HEN THE ÊUMP COMMAND IS CALLED THE TRACK AND SECTOR FOR  THE           BLOCK ARE READ FROM THE BYTE UNDER THE CURSOR  AND  THE  NEXT           BYTE RESPECTIVELY. ÔHE PROGRAM WILL GO TO THE  DISK  DRIVE  ,           GET THE DATA FROM THE NEW BLOCK AND DISPLAY IT ON THE SCREEN.           ÔHIS COMMAND IS USEFUL WHEN FOLLOWING THE FORWARD LINKS OF  A           FILE STARTING FROM A DIRECTORY ENTRY.               3.Ë  'Î'  ÎEXT           ÔHE ÎEXT COMMAND IS ENVOKED BY DEPRESSING THE 'N' KEY.           ×HEN THE ÎEXT COMMAND IS CALLED THE TRACK AND SECTOR FOR  THE           BLOCK ARE READ FROM BYTE  0  AND  BYTE  1  RESPECTIVELY.  ÔHE           PROGRAM WILL GO TO THE DISK DRIVE , GET THE DATA FROM THE NEW           BLOCK AND DISPLAY IT ON THE SCREEN.   ÔHIS  COMMAND  IS  VERY           USEFUL WHEN FOLLOWING THE FORWARD LINKS OF A FILE.                                                                  PAGE 8                                               ÄISK ÄOCTOR ÄOCUMENTATION               3.0    ÃOMMANDS               3.Ë  'Ò'  ÒEWRITE ÂLOCK TO ÆLOPPY           ÔHE ÒEWRITE COMMAND IS ENVOKED BY DEPRESSING THE 'R' KEY.           ×HEN THE CHANGE BYTE COMMAND IS CALLED A PROMPT IS PRINTED IN           THE MESSAGE BUFFER UNDER THE DATA BOX AS FOLLOWS :                      ÒÅ×ÒÉÔÅ ÂÌÏÃË  ÁÒÅ ÙÏÕ ÓÕÒÅ [Y/N]           ÔHE PROGRAM IS NOW WAITING FOR YOU TO ANSWER 'Y' TO CONTINUE.           ÉF YOU ANSWER YES TO THIS PROMPT THE DATA FROM THE  DATA  BOX           WILL BE WRITTEN TO THE FLOPPY DISKETTE IN IT'S  PRESENT  FORM           WHETHER  IT  WAS  ALTERED  OR  NOT.    ÏF   COURSE   IF   THE           WRITE-PROTECT NOTCH IS COVERED THE ATTEMPT TO  WRITE  TO  THE           DISK WILL FAIL.  ÄEPRESSING ANY  KEY  (INCLUDING  THE  'ÓÔÏÐ'           KEY) BUT THE 'Y' KEY WILL ABORT THE ÒEWRITE FUNCTION.               3.Í  'Ð'  ÐRINT THE SECTOR           ÔHE ÐRINT COMMAND IS ENVOKED BY DEPRESSING THE 'P' KEY.           ×HEN THE PRINT COMMAND IS CALLED A PROMPT IS PRINTED  IN  THE           MESSAGE BUFFER UNDER THE DATA BOX AS FOLLOWS :                      ÈÅØ ÄÕÍÐ ÔÏ ÐÒÉÎÔÅÒ    ? [Y/N]           ÔHE PROGRAM IS NOW WAITING FOR YOU TO ANSWER 'Y' TO CONTINUE.           ÉF YOU ANSWER YES TO THIS PROMPT THE PRINTER WILL  PRINT  THE           HEXIDECIMAL VALUES AND OF THE DATA BOX AS WELL  AS  AN  ÁÓÃÉÉ           REPRESENTATION OF THE DATA.  ÐRESSING ANY KEY OTHER THAN  THE           'Y' KEY WILL ABORT THE PRINT FUNCTION.           ÉF THERE IS A PROBLEM WITH THE PRINTER (IE. NOT CONNECTED  OR           TURNED OFF) A PROMPT WILL BE PRINTED IN  THE  MESSAGE  BUFFER           UNDER THE DATA BOX AS FOLLOWS :                      ÎÏ ÐÒÉÎÔÅÒ ÃÏÎÎÅÃÔÅÄ           ÉN THIS CASE DEPRESSING  ANY  KEY  WILL  RETURN  YOU  TO  THE           COMMAND MODE.                                                                  PAGE 9                                               ÄISK ÄOCTOR ÄOCUMENTATION               3.0    ÃOMMANDS               3.Î  'ÈÅÌÐ' ÈELP           ÔHE ÈELP FUNCTION IS ENVOKED BY DEPRESSING THE 'ÈÅÌÐ' KEY.           ×HEN THE ÈELP FUNCTION IS CALLED A SCREEN FULL OF INFORMATION           CONTAINING A QUICK SUMMARY WILL APPEAR.  ÄEPRESSING  ANY  KEY           AT THIS POINT WILL RETURN YOU TO WHERE YOU LEFT.               3.Ï  'Æ1' ÆUNCTION ËEY           ÔHE Æ1 FUNCTION IS ENVOKED BY DEPRESSING THE 'Æ1' KEY.           ×HEN THE Æ1 FUNCTION IS CALLED, THIS WILL CAUSE  THE  PROGRAM    